.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt LOCALE 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm locale
.Nd report locale categories
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a | Fl m | Fl k
.Op Ar category ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility resolves the environment through the locale state and reports locale information.
Without options or operands it prints
.Ev LANG ,
each
.Ev LC_*
category, the raw
.Ev LC_ALL
value and
.Cm codeset
from
.Xr nl_langinfo 3 .
An unset environment falls back to
.Ql C.UTF-8 .
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
List known locales:
.Ql C ,
.Ql POSIX
and
.Ql C.UTF-8 .
.It Fl m
List known charmaps:
.Ql ANSI_X3.4-1968
and
.Ql UTF-8 .
.It Fl k
List the keyword names:
.Ql LANG ,
the six
.Ql LC_*
categories,
.Ql LC_ALL
and
.Ql codeset .
.El
.Pp
A category operand prints one
.Ql NAME="value"
line.
.Ql LANG
prints the raw environment value and
.Ql LC_ALL
prints the resolved composite.
Unknown categories are an error. Options and category operands are mutually exclusive.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for an unknown category, 2 for usage.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr iconv 1 ,
.Xr gencat 1
.Sh STANDARDS
A documented subset of POSIX
.Nm locale .
This build knows only the C, POSIX and C.UTF-8 names; locale-archive discovery,
.Fl c ,
.Fl u ,
.Fl v
and target execution are unsupported.
